 },
 "limits": "Retail leaves the final stop_flag in EAX (mov eax,[esi+0x2c] before pop/ret), but the recovered contract is void: no recovered caller reads EAX after Qvm_ExecuteInstructions. return_value is therefore normalized to null on both sides and the loop state is verified through instruction_offset, stop_flag and error_status instead. The opcode handlers are synthetic: retail handler-table first dwords are redirected to a sentinel trap so each real dispatch site is observed, and both sides apply the same advance/raise policy. The state pointer and code_base are opaque synthetic addresses; the retail 24-byte opcode table and the 64-bit host handler-array layout are never compared byte for byte.",
